silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_04_shared_diagram_decomposition_step__step_f_v_view_functor a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "F_v is a view functor: a typed function from the local olog category C to a rendering category (formal equations, PDF diagrams, plain-English paragraphs, source-index tables). Each view v produces a different rendering of the same underlying Mittens colimit." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_04_shared_diagram_decomposition_step__step_colimf_v_circ_d_mittens_preservation_of_colimit_under_view_f a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "colim(F_v circ D_Mittens) is the colimit of the composed diagram: first apply F_v to each object in D_Mittens, then compute the colimit in the rendering category. The isomorphism kappa: colim(F_v circ D_Mittens) -> F_v(Mittens) is the comparison map." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_04_shared_diagram_decomposition_step__step_functor_preservation_of_colimits_joc_§13 a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "JoC §13: a functor F: C -> D preserves a colimit if the comparison map kappa: colim(F circ D) -> F(colim D) is an isomorphism. Left adjoints preserve all colimits. The multi-view agreement theorem requires each view functor to preserve the D_Mittens colimit." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_04_shared_diagram_decomposition_step__step_four_view_instance_for_mittens_cocone a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Formal view: the twelve-leg theorem with tikzcd diagram. Diagram view: the shared MittensColimitCocone TikZ figure. Reader view: 'Mittens-the-cat is assembled from twelve distinct typed observations: health record, microchip ID, body-mass quality, weight measurement, value 3450, unit grams, pet role, sleep process, SHACL validation receipt, audit trail, DomesticCat classification, and Felis catus TSN 183798 taxonomy.' Source view: the witnesses.csv ledger with twelve rows." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_04_shared_diagram_decomposition_step__step_yoneda_inheritance_of_multi_view_contract a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "By Yoneda naturality, every downstream paper that claims a dense mathematical result must produce at least two synchronized views. The multi-view agreement law transports from the spine to every sibling paper via the Chapter 12 spine-inheritance arrows." .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_sections_04_shared_diagram_decomposition_step__step_multi_view_agreement_recap a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Every dense claim must appear in at least two synchronized views (formal + diagram + reader + source); the four views must agree at the Mittens apex; the multi-view contract is inherited by all 41 sibling papers via Yoneda naturality; a diagram that shows an edge absent from the formal theorem fails the contract." .
